+    * a thread may already be blocked in the kernel waiting for them (zink
+    * waits for its batch timeline point with no timeout).  Signal them so it
+    * wakes up; the runtime's post-wait vk_device_check_status() then returns
+    * VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST to it, as it does to every later wait.
